{ The Pirc Defense is a sharp hypermodern opening which leads to aggressive plays. The main idea of this opening is for Black to slowly develop pawns and pieces, tempting White to build a 'solid' pawn center in the middle. Black proceeds to counterstrike White's overextended pawn center and if White does not respond accurately, he literally self-destructs. lol. }
1. e4 d6 { White greedily takes the center } 2. d4 { Black develops his Knight and later on, fianchettoes his Bishop in hopes of early castling while attacking White's e4 pawn } 2... Nf6 { White defends with Nc3 } { [%cal Gf6e4] } 3. Nc3 { Black prepares to fianchetto his Bishop } { [%cal Gc3e4,Gf6e4] } 3... g6 { And this is the Pirc Defense! Here, Black has a very solid position with minimal weaknesses as both his pawns have only advanced one rank. White's downfall is trying to occupy as much space as possible while accidentally overextending his pieces! } *


