{ The Austrian Attack is characterised by f4, White's attempt to dominate the center }
4. f4 { Black's plan is to counterstrike White's overextended center with d5, but first, he needs to play c6 to support his coming pawn break } { [%cal Gd6d5,Gc7c6] } 4... c6 { White's plan is to put his Knight behind his pawns and attack our Kingside! } { [%cal Gg1f3,Gf4f5,Ge4e5] } 5. Nf3 { Now, Black can finally challenge White's center! } 5... d5 *


